  "description": "This dataset provides multimodal neuroimaging data from 53 healthy young adults performing a probabilistic decision-making task involving risk and ambiguity. It combines structural MRI (T1w, T2w, DWI), functional MRI acquired during task performance, and concurrent EEG recordings during inhibitory TMS applied over parietal regions and the vertex. The dataset aims to elucidate the role of the parietal cortex and its interactions with other brain regions in decision-making under uncertainty.",
  "methods_description": "Data include structural MRI (T1w, T2w, DWI) and task-based fMRI, together with concurrent EEG recordings collected during inhibitory transcranial magnetic stimulation (TMS) applied over two parietal regions and the vertex, in 53 healthy volunteers aged 18-31 performing a decision-making task under risk and ambiguity.",
